#+TITLE: @geordi — analytics-infrastructure console
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: geordi-console
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:geordi:specialist:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# The first persistent Layer 2 specialist console for org-llm. Owned
# by =@geordi= (alias =@analyst=, TNG chief engineer) — analytics
# *infrastructure* health, not the data flowing through it. Where
# =@picard='s Captain's Bridge is one chart per vital sign, this
# console goes deeper on a narrower slice: the LLM call layer + the
# crew-log audit. Every metric expression is verbatim from
# =org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml=.

* Tail latency by model
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Worst-case wall-clock duration of LLM calls per =model= per day —
the P99-shaped lens the Captain's mean-latency bar can't surface.
A single 60-second outlier on =qwen2.5-coder= won't move the
captain's average but will dominate this line; that's the point.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name tail_latency_by_model :metric llm_max_ms :group_by [model, llm_day]
SELECT model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS llm_day, MAX(duration_ms) AS llm_max_ms
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Mean latency drift
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Mean call duration per =model= per day. The captain shows mean
latency once (call_kind × model snapshot); =@geordi= tracks it
across time so context-bloat regressions and model-swap
performance shifts are visible as slope changes, not as a single
bar that may already be polluted with last week's data.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name mean_latency_drift :metric llm_avg_ms :group_by [model, llm_day]
SELECT model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS llm_day, AVG(duration_ms) AS llm_avg_ms
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Embed vs chat throughput
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Total LLM calls per =call_kind= per day. The captain measures
*latency* by =call_kind= but not *volume* — an embed pipeline
stall or a chat-turn explosion shows up here first as a
collapsing or runaway bar before either error-rate or latency
notices.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name embed_vs_chat_throughput :metric llm_calls :group_by [call_kind, llm_day]
SELECT call_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS llm_day, COUNT(*) AS llm_calls
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY call_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Crew action mix
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Manager (crew) audit-log rows by =crew_action= × =crew_outcome=.
The captain's fan-out heatmap answers "who talks to whom";
=@geordi='s answers "what kind of work and did it succeed". A fat
=delegate / not-ok= cell is the infra-quality signal — the manager
is dispatching but specialists are failing the handoff.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name crew_action_mix :metric crew_actions :group_by [crew_action, crew_outcome]
SELECT action AS crew_action, outcome AS crew_outcome, COUNT(*) AS crew_actions
FROM crew_log
GROUP BY action, outcome
#+END_SRC

# Run:
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/@geordi-console.org.example \
#       --emit-only /tmp/geordi-console.zip
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/@geordi-console.org.example \
#       --post http://localhost:8088
